---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- Every address on the site that search engines should be offered.

    The list is built from Eleventy's "all" collection rather than written
    out by hand, so a new page or post appears here the moment it is added
    and nothing has to be remembered at the time.

    Two kinds of page are kept out. The redirect pages generated by
    redirects.njk exclude themselves from collections, so they never reach
    this list at all: they exist only to forward old WordPress addresses,
    and each one already carries a noindex tag. The 404 page is filtered
    out below, because a sitemap is a list of pages worth visiting.

    lastmod is given for blog posts only. A post carries a real date in its
    front matter, so the value means something. The ordinary pages have no
    date of their own, and Eleventy would fall back to the file's timestamp
    — which on the build server is just the moment the repository was
    checked out, so every page would claim to have changed on every deploy. -#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for item in collections.all %}
{%- if item.url != "/404.html" %}
  <url>
    <loc>https://amirkhesro.com{{ item.url }}</loc>
{%- if item.url.startsWith("/blog/") and item.url != "/blog/" %}
    <lastmod>{{ item.date | htmlDate }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
  </url>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
